    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days` in `solution.py` and wrote 28 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (28 passed). I did not measure coverage, but every line of `solution.py` is reached by the tests, so the 90% gate should pass.\n\nThe implementation steps one day at a time, skipping weekends and holidays, in the direction given by the sign of `n`. For `n == 0` it advances to the next business day only when `start` is not one. Holidays are copied into a set up front, so a generator is consumed once and validated before any date arithmetic. `start` and `n` are type-checked, with `datetime` rejected wherever a `date` is expected and `bool` rejected for `n`. The tests cover forward and backward movement across weekends, holidays on and around the start date, weekend holidays, the `n == 0` cases, and each `TypeError` path. I checked the expected dates by hand against the calendar, since 2026-11-14 is a Saturday.",
